    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Protect the camera. Explain the missed moment.",
        "accent": "amber",
        "text": [
          "Proposed teaching design \u00b7 not Ring firmware behavior. Temperatures and restart gates are illustrative device-body values, not outdoor-weather limits.",
          "The doorbell contains Camera and an always-on Controller. Health telemetry survives camera shutdown in this design, enabling the illustrated notices. Both views follow the same complete steps. Source: docs/hlds/thermal-doorbell.md."
